+# Delivery Plan
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Milestone | Start | End |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| kickoff | 2026-08-24 | 2026-08-26 |
+| requirements | 2026-08-27 | 2026-09-07 |
+| architecture | 2026-09-08 | 2026-09-14 |
+| build-core | 2026-09-15 | 2026-10-01 |
+| build-integrations | 2026-10-02 | 2026-10-15 |
+| hardening | 2026-10-16 | 2026-10-23 |
+| acceptance | 2026-10-26 | 2026-10-29 |
+| launch | 2026-10-30 | 2026-11-02 |
+
+## Countdown
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Business days until kickoff | 5 |
+| Total business days | 48 |
+
+## Notes
+
+The plan is a strict serial sequence: each milestone starts on the next
+business day after the previous one ends, so there is no slack anywhere in the
+schedule — 48 business days of milestones tile 48 consecutive business days
+from 2026-08-24 through 2026-11-02. Build work dominates the middle: build-core
+(12 days) and build-integrations (9 days) together account for nearly half the
+calendar, landing between mid-September and mid-October.
+
+All three company holidays fall inside the build phases: 2026-08-31 stretches
+requirements across the Labor Day week, 2026-09-25 lands mid-build-core, and
+2026-10-12 falls inside build-integrations. The heavy phases absorb them
+cleanly, but the flip side of zero slack is that any overrun pushes launch
+day-for-day; the one-weekend launch (starting Friday 2026-10-30) also means the
+final go-live decision lands on Monday 2026-11-02 rather than end of week.
